D2 - unspecified evaluation order of random draws (Docs/PERFORMANCE.md, section 6.4).

Seven expressions draw two random numbers inside function arguments or operands whose evaluation
order C++ leaves unspecified (GCC evaluates right to left, Clang left to right), so GCC and Clang
builds give different worlds for the same seed. The patch draws them into locals first, in GCC's
order, so GCC results are unchanged and Clang (and MSVC) reproduce them.

Not applied: Source/NoctisCore/Private/Creatures belongs to another work stream. Made against commit
5eabfd4; also applies (with line offsets) to the working copy of 16 October 2026, 04:30.
Apply from the repository root with:  git apply Docs/patches/D2_rng_evaluation_order.diff

